* C:\users\christoph\Documents\git\MegawattKS_Radio_Design_101\VFO\vackar\simulation\design5.asc
J1 N003 N006 0 J309
L1 N001 N003 4.7µ Rser=10
R1 N006 0 4.7k
C1 N002 N006 150p
C2 0 N006 10p
L2 N003 N002 100n Rser=0.2
V1 N001 0 5
C3 N003 0 120p
R2 osc_out 0 10k
C4 osc_out N003 100n
C5 N002 N005 150p
R3 N005 N004 10k
V2 N004 0 3
D1 0 N005 1SV324
D2 0 N005 1SV324
D3 0 N005 1SV324
.model D D
.lib C:\users\christoph\Documents\LTspiceXVII\lib\cmp\standard.dio
.model NJF NJF
.model PJF PJF
.lib C:\users\christoph\Documents\LTspiceXVII\lib\cmp\standard.jft
.tran 0 100u 50u 1n
.param first_edge 200 ; 200th edge
.param last_edge 700 ; 700th edge
.param zero_crossing_voltage 0 ; voltage at zero crossing
.meas tran T1 find time when V(osc_out)={zero_crossing_voltage} rise {first_edge}
.meas tran T2 find time when V(osc_out)={zero_crossing_voltage} rise {last_edge}
.meas tran Frequency param ({last_edge}-{first_edge})/(T2-T1)
.options numdgt=7
.options plotwinsize=0
.model 1SV324 D(Is=2.593E-15 Rs=0.4 N=1.024 BV=10 Ibv=1.00E-04 Cjo=7.672E-11 Vj=100 M=49.19)
* Voltage over varicaps must be limited, so that means that they should be quite large\nin comparison to the capacitors in series.\nUnfortunately, in a series capacitor network, the largest capacitor doesn't have a lot \nof influence on the frequency.
.backanno
.end
